agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md:505:| `workspace_inspect` | R | The one read for current state. `sections` selects any of: `summary` (default: project identity and saved state, printer pointer, intent line, selection ids, plate and object counts, plan headline, top unresolved warning); `project` (description, designer, license, safety and usage notes, assembly, bill of materials, profile notes, attachment list, versions and recovery state, each with provenance); `intent` (the intent record with provenance and an `unanswered` list); `printer` (the selected printer: configured versus observed nozzle, plate, and filaments with timestamps, computed `mismatches`, `confirmedFacts`, job progress, temperatures, alerts, monitoring policy); `objects` (plates, objects, parts, instances, extruder, quantity, bounding box, override and region counts, print order; `printable` is true when every copy prints, which needs the object's own switch and each copy's, and a row whose `printable` is false adds `printableInstanceCount`, the copies that still print, so a copy switched off in the object list reads differently from an object `plate_layout` disabled); `plan` (the pinned plan, deviations from the profile, estimates when a slice is valid); `slicing` (state and action handle per plate, progress, invalidation); `level` concise or detail. | workspace snapshot; `MachineObject`; `PresetBundle`; JusPrin stores; `UndoRedo` | per section: 4 KB text fields, 64 attachments, 16 slots and alerts, 64 objects with cursor |
agent-docs/jusprin/mcp-tool-extension-guide.md:511:| `setup_record` | M | In-app only. Records the chat's setup in one call: `purpose` (required on every call) is what the user wants the print to be or do, in a few words and their terms, not how to print it, and titles the setup card; optional `fields` over the intent record (`assumed` for the agent's inferences; only values grounded in the user's statement become `user_confirmed`); the plan, flat beside them: the agent's own statement of how it will print (`headline`, the strategy; `decisions` with confidence and alternatives; `unverified`, what it took as true without checking, one sentence each; `risks`), which replaces the whole plan when a headline is given and is kept when there is none. The plan is not a nested object: DeepSeek V4 Flash sent one as a string of JSON, which the registry refuses. Applies no setting. | JusPrin intent and plan stores | 60-character purpose, 32 fields, 2 KB per field, 16 decisions |
